    String raw = request.getTelephone();
    String e164 = TelephoneNormalizer.toE164(raw);
    if (e164 == null) {
        throw new InvalidTelephoneException(raw);
    }
    request.setTelephone(e164);
}
```

**`EnsureUniqueTelephone.java`** — scans `ownerRepository.findAll()`, comparing each existing owner's E.164 telephone; throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` (409) on collision.
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateTelephoneException {
    String telephone = request.getTelephone();
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (telephone.equals(TelephoneNormalizer.toE164(existing.getTelephone()))) {
            throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(telephone);
        }
    }
}
```

**`NormalizeOwnerEmail.java`** — email is optional; if present it must match a simple email regex, else `InvalidEmailException` (400); stores lower-cased trimmed value back on the shared request.
```java
private static final Pattern EMAIL = Pattern.compile("^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$");

public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws InvalidEmailException {
    String raw = request.getEmail();
    if (raw == null || raw.isBlank()) {
        return;
    }
    String trimmed = raw.trim();
    if (!EMAIL.matcher(trimmed).matches()) {
        throw new InvalidEmailException(raw);
    }
    request.setEmail(trimmed.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT));
}
```

**`BuildOwner.java`** — maps the request DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper.toOwner(request)`, publishes `Out<Owner>`.
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
    built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
}
```

**`DefaultRegistrationDate.java`** — if `registrationDate` is null, sets it to `LocalDate.now()`; mutates `@Val Owner` in place.
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
    }
}
```

**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** — assigns `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` where NNNN = `findAll().size()+1` zero-padded to 4 digits.
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    int sequence = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1;
    owner.setCustomerCode(format(owner.getLastName(), sequence));
}
private static String format(String lastName, int sequence) {
    String prefix = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();
    return String.format("%s-%04d", prefix, sequence);
}
```

**`SaveOwner.java`** — persists via `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

**`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** — maps to `OwnerDto` and returns 201 Created with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
    OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
}
```

**Supporting helper (not directly in YAML but used by two of the above):** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/TelephoneNormalizer.java` — package-private static `toE164(String)`: strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps leading `+`/country code, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; result must be `+` followed by 8–15 digits or returns null.

### 3. Owner entity

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** — `@Entity @Table(name="owners")`, extends `Person`. Fields:
- `firstName`, `lastName` — inherited from `Person` (`@NotEmpty`)
- `address` (`@NotEmpty`), `city` (`@NotEmpty`)
- `telephone` (`@NotEmpty`, `@Pattern` requiring E.164 `^\+[0-9]{8,15}$`)
- `email` (nullable)
- `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`)
- `customerCode` (`String`)
- `pets` (`@OneToMany`, EAGER, cascade ALL)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`** — `@MappedSuperclass` extending `BaseEntity`, holds `firstName` and `lastName` (both `@NotEmpty`, `protected`).

### 4. Request body DTO — `OwnerFieldsDto`

This DTO is **generated at build time** from the OpenAPI spec (there is no hand-written `.java` for it; the schema is the source of truth). Defined in **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** as schema `OwnerFields` (lines 1991–2054). Generated class name: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto`.

Properties: `firstName` (1–30, letters/space/'/- pattern), `lastName` (1–30, similar pattern with optional trailing dot), `address` (1–255), `city` (1–80), `telephone` (1–20, `^[0-9]*$`), `email` (optional, ≤255), `registrationDate` (optional, date). Required: firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone. (Full schema shown above in the openapi excerpt.)

### 5. Response DTO — `OwnerDto`

Also generated from **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**, schema `Owner` (lines 2055–2099). Generated class: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerDto`. It is `allOf` `OwnerFields` plus read-only fields: `id` (int32), `displayName` ("LastName, FirstName"), `initials` ("G.F."), `customerCode` ("<LAST3>-<NNNN>"), and required `pets` (array of `Pet`). The `displayName` and `initials` are computed in the mapper.

**Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — MapStruct `@Mapper(uses = PetMapper.class)`. Relevant methods: `toOwnerDto(Owner)` (adds `displayName`/`initials` via expressions), `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (ignores `id` and `pets`), plus collection/page variants. `OwnerPageDto` (schema `OwnerPage`) is also used for paged listing.

### 6. OwnerRepository interface

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`**

Existing query methods:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int id)`
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()`
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

All declared `throws DataAccessException`. Note there is **no** query method for telephone, city, address, or household — uniqueness/count logic in the create flow is done by iterating `findAll()`. Implementations exist at: `repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, and `repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`.

### 7. Escalation handlers — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`

Each YAML maps an exception type to a handler class (all one-liners `handle: class: ...`):

| YAML file | Handler class |
|---|---|
| `...escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml` | `MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler` (400) |
| `...escalation.DuplicateTelephoneException.yml` | `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler` (409) |
| `...escalation.InvalidTelephoneException.yml` | `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` (400) |
| `...escalation.InvalidEmailException.yml` | `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler` (400) |
| `...escalation.NotFoundException.yml` | `NotFoundExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml` | `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` | `ValidationExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml` | `ForbiddenExceptionHandler` |
| `java.lang.Exception.yml` | `GeneralExceptionHandler` (catch-all) |

Owner-creation-related ones (contents shown):

- **`MissingOwnerFieldsException`** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/.../rest/escalation/MissingOwnerFieldsException.java` (holds `List<String> missingFields`) and its handler responds 400 with a ProblemDetail whose `errors` property = the missing field names.
- **`DuplicateTelephoneException`** — holds `telephone`; handler responds 409, ProblemDetail `telephone` property = conflicting value.
- **`InvalidTelephoneException`** — holds `rejectedValue`; handler responds 400, ProblemDetail `rejectedValue` property.
- **`InvalidEmailException`** — holds `rejectedValue`; handler responds 400, ProblemDetail `rejectedValue` property.

All handlers follow the same shape: `handle(@Parameter <Exception> ex, ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>> response)`, building the body via the shared helper **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/.../rest/escalation/ProblemDetails.java`** (`build(ex, status, detail)` sets type `about:blank`, title = exception simple name, timestamp, and an empty `schemaValidationErrors` list). Their file paths are all in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/`.

### 8. Owner-creation tests

Tests live in **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`**:
- `AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box base (SpringBootTest + MockMvc, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser` admin). Provides the POST helpers `createOwner(body)` → `mvc.perform(post("/api/owners")...)`, `createOwnerOk(body)` (asserts 2xx and returns id), `createOwnerWithKey(...)`, `ownerNode()` (fully valid unique payload), and readers `getOwner(id)`/`fetchOwner(id)`.
- `AcceptanceTest.java` — the actual POST /owners creation tests.
- `AuditLogCapture.java` — audit support.

`AcceptanceTest.java` (full contents):
```java
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreRejectsSameLastNameAndAddress() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText()); b.put("address", a.get("address").asText());
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());
	}

	@Test
	void functionalityAllowsDifferentAddress() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText());
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
	}

	@Test
	void functionalityAllowsWithSharesHousehold() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText()); b.put("address", a.get("address").asText());
		b.put("sharesHousehold", true);
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
	}
}
```

Note: these acceptance tests exercise a "household-duplicate" rule (reject same lastName + same address unless `sharesHousehold=true`), and the base helpers reference forward-looking fields (`postcode`, `addressLine1`, `sharesHousehold`, `Idempotency-Key`). None of that logic exists in the current POST /owners YAML chain or functions — the current flow only enforces required-fields, telephone normalization + E.164 uniqueness, email normalization, registration-date defaulting, and customer-code assignment. So these tests describe target behavior not yet implemented in the current create flow.

